// Closures whose record is built in the function being optimised.
//
// A closure record (a slot marked Closure) holds the closure's code pointer
// and the addresses of the variables it captures. Lowering writes each
// word once, with a value that is the same whenever the store runs, and
// nothing writes to the record afterwards. So a load from the record is the
// value stored at the same offset, wherever the load is, even across calls
// that receive the record's address. Once the closure's code is known at a
// call through it, the inliner can inline the call (inline.go); once the
// inlined body's loads of captured addresses are forwarded, the variables
// are reached directly, and when nothing reads the record any more its
// stores go, which lets SROA and mem2reg promote the captured variables.

